# J24 — Remediation lifecycle reality (fixture target — monorepo is NEVER
# patched; every patch action here runs against the harness fixture repo).
#
# Drives the runtime-free remediation truth end-to-end on a real git fixture:
# a real finding, a durable defer-with-reason (peer outcome, not a dead end),
# and the HONEST patch refusals — an unconfirmed finding refuses drafting,
# and a confirmed finding without a configured model runtime refuses with
# the explicit no-silent-fallback message instead of pretending a draft
# exists. The Fix page renders the remediation lifecycle summary with its
# distinct states. Model-backed draft→staged→applied→reverified requires a
# configured model runtime; on a runtime-less box those states are
# unreachable BY DESIGN and the refusal captures are the honest record.
name: Remediation lifecycle reality (fixture target)
size: 120x36
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
shell: rm -rf "@TMP_TARGET/.kuzushi" && git -C "@TMP_TARGET" add -A >/dev/null 2>&1; git -C "@TMP_TARGET" -c user.email=devex@kuzushi -c user.name=kz-devex commit -qm fixture >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 30 KUZUSHI
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
wait: 2
submit: run secret-scan:scan {}
wait-for: 60 run receipt
wait: 2
submit: findings
wait-live-snap: 15 Viewing Review | review-fixture-finding
expect: candidate
expect: claim ·
# An unconfirmed finding refuses patch drafting — triage gates remediation.
submit: run patch:finding {"fingerprint":"F-0001"}
wait-for: 30 run receipt
wait: 1
snap: patch-refusal-unconfirmed
ask: Refusal — does patch:finding on an untriaged finding state WHY it refuses (triage first) instead of failing opaquely?
# The remediation lifecycle summary distinguishes the four states (plus the
# durable defer path) — audited while the triptych owns the page.
nav-mode:
keys: 5
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Fix | fix-lifecycle
expect: patch drafted
expect: applied
expect: proof fails after patch
expect: defer with a reason code
ask: Fix — does the remediation summary distinguish draft / staged / applied / reverified states?
# Confirm the finding, then patch again: the refusal moves to the missing
# model runtime with the explicit no-silent-fallback message.
nav-mode:
keys: 3
wait: 1
submit: decision confirmed fixture credential confirmed for the lifecycle audit
wait: 1
# On a confirmed finding, drafting first crosses the explicit authorization
# gate (descriptor-declared repository-execute effect), then refuses with
# the specific missing prerequisite: patching requires a TRIAGE verdict,
# not just a review decision.
submit: run patch:finding {"fingerprint":"F-0001"}
wait-for: 20 CONFIRM · descriptor-declared effect
snap: patch-authorization-gate
expect: patch:finding
keys: y
wait-for: 30 run receipt
wait: 1
nav-mode:
keys: 5
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Fix | patch-refusal-untriaged
expect: has no triage verdict
# Discard the refused attempt (evidence stays on disk) so the remediation
# triptych is visible again for the lifecycle-state audit below.
keys: d
wait: 1
# Defer-with-reason is a durable PEER outcome, reachable without a runtime.
submit: proof defer F-0001 --reason fixture credential rotates with the lab; patch deferred to phase 2
wait: 2
snap: proof-deferred
expect: proof deferred for F-0001
# The deferral is durable: the prove surface reports it as a recorded peer
# outcome, not a dismissed prompt.
nav-mode:
keys: 4
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Prove | prove-after-defer
ask: Prove — is the recorded deferral visible as a durable outcome for this finding?
